{{!
    @template core/user_menu_metadata

    User menu metadata template, overridden by Dimensions.

    Modification compared to the original template:
    * Show the user's name beside the avatar in the navbar, from the md breakpoint up, so the
      session is identified at a glance. Core renders only the avatar here and keeps the name
      inside the open menu. The name is dimensionsnavname, the identity field the administrator
      chose for the navbar, already masked by its display pattern (plain text, escaped here); a
      context without that key shows core's userfullname, whatever fullname() composes under the
      site's fullnamedisplay setting.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * metadata - Array of extra badges (logged in as, failed logins), each with classes and content
    * avatardata - Array of avatars, each with classes and content
    * userfullname - The name of the logged in user, as core composed it
    * dimensionsnavname - The name the navbar shows, when the theme's renderer wrote one

    Example context (json):
    {
        "metadata": [
            {
                "classes": "loginfailures",
                "content": "1 failed login attempt"
            }
        ],
        "avatardata": [
            {
                "classes": "current",
                "content": "<span class=\"userpicture\"></span>"
            }
        ],
        "userfullname": "Antônio Perovano",
        "dimensionsnavname": "Cel. Perovano"
    }
}}
{{#metadata}}
    <span class="usertext d-flex me-3">
        <span class="meta d-flex {{classes}}">
            {{{content}}}
        </span>
    </span>
{{/metadata}}
<span class="avatars">
    {{#avatardata}}
        <span class="avatar {{classes}}">
            {{{content}}}
        </span>
    {{/avatardata}}
</span>
{{#dimensionsnavname}}
    <span class="dimensions-usermenu-name d-none d-md-inline">{{dimensionsnavname}}</span>
{{/dimensionsnavname}}
{{^dimensionsnavname}}
    {{#userfullname}}
        <span class="dimensions-usermenu-name d-none d-md-inline">{{userfullname}}</span>
    {{/userfullname}}
{{/dimensionsnavname}}
